        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mcp): bound CLI OAuth login through guarded fetch timeout",
        "body": "<details>\n<summary>Additional instructions</summary>\n\n**MUST:** Keep **Allow edits from maintainers** enabled for this PR so maintainers\ncan help update the branch when needed.\n\n</details>\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators running `openclaw mcp login <name>` could see the OAuth login workflow hang indefinitely when the MCP server, OAuth discovery endpoint, or an upstream proxy stopped responding during the CLI login flow.\n\nBefore this patch, `mcp login` built an HTTP `fetchFn` via `buildMcpHttpFetch(...)` but did not pass the configured MCP `requestTimeoutMs` into the guarded fetch lifecycle. A stalled remote endpoint could leave the login command waiting forever with no deadline.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nApply the configured MCP `requestTimeoutMs` at the owning guarded HTTP fetch boundary: `mcp login` now passes `requestTimeoutMs: resolved.requestTimeoutMs` into `buildMcpHttpFetch`, which forwards it to `fetchWithSsrFGuard` as `timeoutMs` and keeps timeout refresh/cleanup tied to the managed response body stream. This replaces the earlier OAuth-only `wrapFetchWithTimeout` approach that cleared its timer as soon as response headers returned.\n\nScope stays CLI OAuth login only; broader MCP runtime/session transport timeouts are unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** `openclaw mcp login` could hang forever on a non-responding OAuth/discovery endpoint even when the MCP server had a configured timeout.\n\n**After:** Configured MCP `requestTimeoutMs` values apply to CLI OAuth login HTTP requests through the guarded MCP fetch lifecycle; stalled endpoints abort with `TimeoutError` instead of blocking the operator indefinitely.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `src/agents/mcp-http-fetch.ts` — optional `requestTimeoutMs` forwarded to guarded fetch `timeoutMs`\n- `src/cli/mcp-cli.ts` — `mcp login` passes `requestTimeoutMs: resolved.requestTimeoutMs` into `buildMcpHttpFetch`\n- Regression: `src/agents/mcp-http-fetch.test.ts` — hung-request timeout via guarded fetch\n- Caller-path regression: `src/cli/mcp-cli.test.ts` — login wires `requestTimeoutMs: 9_000` into `buildMcpHttpFetch`\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** CLI MCP OAuth login no longer leaves OAuth HTTP requests unbounded when the remote endpoint stops responding before headers return; configured login timeouts abort with `TimeoutError` through the guarded MCP fetch lifecycle.\n- **Canonical reachability path:** Operator runs `openclaw mcp login <name>` → `registerMcpCli` login handler → `resolveMcpTransportConfig` reads `requestTimeoutMs` → `buildMcpHttpFetch({ requestTimeoutMs })` → `fetchWithSsrFGuard({ timeoutMs })` → `runMcpOAuthLogin({ fetchFn })` → MCP SDK `auth(...)` OAuth HTTP fetch receives abort at deadline.\n- **Boundary crossed:** local-runtime; production `buildMcpHttpFetch` + `mcp login` wiring exercised via colocated Vitest (no live stalled OAuth server in this environment).\n- **Shared helper / provider constraint check:** Reuses existing guarded fetch timeout/refresh lifecycle in `fetchWithSsrFGuard` + `wrapGuardedBodyStream`; provider constraints N/A because this is CLI-local OAuth login HTTP wrapping.\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS, Node 22, source checkout on branch `codex/mcp-login-timeout`.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/mcp-http-fetch.test.ts src/cli/mcp-cli.test.ts -t \"aborts hung OAuth|configures enablement, timeouts, and OAuth login\" --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n\n```text\n ✓ aborts hung OAuth requests when requestTimeoutMs is configured\n ✓ configures enablement, timeouts, and OAuth login 656ms\n   buildMcpHttpFetch called with requestTimeoutMs: 9000\n\nTest Files  3 passed (3)\n     Tests  3 passed | 49 skipped (52)\n```\n\n- **Observed result after fix:** A hung OAuth fetch aborts at the configured deadline with `TimeoutError`; `mcp login` forwards the configured MCP timeout (`9_000` ms for `--timeout 9`) into `buildMcpHttpFetch`.\n- **What was not tested:** Live `openclaw mcp login` against a real stalled OAuth/discovery endpoint; post-header body stall after partial chunk delivery (guarded fetch refresh is in place, but no dedicated stalled-body Vitest in this environment).\n- **Fix classification:** Root cause fix.\n\n- [x] AI-assisted (Cursor)\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n- Single commit on `upstream/main`\n",
